{"id":"neet-2026r-q140","pn":140,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Placental hormones","q":"Which of the following hormone is not secreted by human placenta?","o":["Estrogen","Progesterone","LH","hCG"],"c":2,"s":"The placenta acts as a temporary endocrine gland in pregnancy.\nIt secretes hCG, human placental lactogen (hPL), estrogen, progestogens and others.\nLH is secreted by the anterior pituitary, not the placenta."},
{"id":"neet-2026r-q141","pn":141,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Spermatozoa","q":"Sperm motility is due to ___________.","o":["ciliary movement","amoeboid movement","muscular movement","flagellar movement"],"c":3,"s":"Sperm travels through the fallopian tube by flagellar movement."},
{"id":"neet-2026-q141","pn":141,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Foetal development","q":"Match List I with List II related to embryonic development at various months of pregnancy:\nA. The foetus movement starts and hair appears on the head — I. 24 weeks of pregnancy\nB. The foetus develops limbs and digits — II. 20 weeks of pregnancy\nC. The foetus develops external genital organs — III. 8 weeks of pregnancy\nD. The foetus body is covered with fine hair; eyelids separate and eyelashes are formed — IV. 12 weeks of pregnancy","o":["A-III, B-II, C-IV, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-III, D-I","A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I"],"c":3,"s":"By the end of the second month (8 weeks) the foetus develops limbs and digits.\nBy the end of 12 weeks (first trimester) most major organ systems are formed; limbs and external genital organs are well developed.\nDuring the fifth month (20 weeks) the first movements of the foetus and hair on the head are usually seen.\nBy about 24 weeks (end of second trimester) the body is covered with fine hair, eyelids separate and eyelashes are formed.\nSo the match is A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I.\nNote: Option 2 is printed as 'A-II, B-III, C-III, D-I' (C-III repeated) in the source; kept as printed. Printed answer is option 4."},
{"id":"neet-2026-q143","pn":143,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Spermatogenesis","q":"Spermatogonia undergo a series of cell divisions statements to produce sperms. Select the correct from the following :\nA. Spermatogonia always undergo meiotic cell division.\nB. Primary spermatocytes divide mitotically to produce secondary spermatocytes.\nC. Secondary spermatocytes, through their second meiotic division, produce haploid spermatids.\nD. Spermatids produce spermatozoa through mitosis.\nE. Spermatids transform into spermatozoa by spermiogenesis.","o":["C and E only","A, C and E only","B, C and D only","A and E only"],"c":0,"s":"A is incorrect: spermatogonia undergo mitotic division.\nB is incorrect: primary spermatocytes undergo the 1st meiotic division to form secondary spermatocytes.\nC is correct: secondary spermatocytes undergo the 2nd meiotic division to form haploid spermatids.\nD is incorrect: spermatids form spermatozoa by a differentiation process called spermiogenesis.\nE is correct: spermatids produce spermatozoa through spermiogenesis.\nSo C and E only are correct."},
{"id":"neet-2026r-q158","pn":158,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Ovulation, oogenesis","q":"The covering of ovum at ovulation is __________.","o":["zona radiata","zona pellucida","chorion","endometrium"],"c":1,"s":"The Graafian follicle ruptures and releases the secondary oocyte (ovum) from the ovary. This is ovulation.\nThe secondary oocyte has a membrane around it called zona pellucida.\nEndometrium is the innermost layer of the uterine wall.\nChorion is the outermost extraembryonic membrane around the embryo."},
{"id":"neet-2026r-q160","pn":160,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Male reproductive system","q":"Which of the following structure is not a part of the male reproductive system?","o":["Epididymis","Vasa efferentia","Infundibulum","Rete testis"],"c":2,"s":"Male accessory ducts include rete testis, vasa efferentia, epididymis and vas deferens.\nOviducts, uterus and vagina are the female accessory ducts.\nInfundibulum is a part of the oviduct."},
{"id":"neet-2026-q161","pn":161,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Structure around the ovum","q":"Arrange the following cell layers/structures around the female gamete, from outer to inner side:\nA. Zona pellucida\nB. Perivitelline space\nC. Corona radiata\nD. Plasma membrane of ovum","o":["C, A, D, B","C, A, B, D","D, B, A, C","A, C, B, D"],"c":1,"s":"From outer to inner side the layers around the female gamete are: corona radiata → zona pellucida → perivitelline space → plasma membrane of ovum.\nSo the answer is C, A, B, D.","fig":{"w":300,"h":232,"alt":"Ovum surrounded by perivitelline space, zona pellucida and cells of the corona radiata, with sperms approaching.","d":[["c",204,125,13,"f"],["c",198.5,151,13,"f"],["c",182.8,172.6,13,"f"],["c",159.8,185.9,13,"f"],["c",133.3,188.6,13,"f"],["c",108,180.4,13,"f"],["c",88.2,162.6,13,"f"],["c",77.4,138.3,13,"f"],["c",77.4,111.7,13,"f"],["c",88.2,87.4,13,"f"],["c",108,69.6,13,"f"],["c",133.3,61.4,13,"f"],["c",159.8,64.1,13,"f"],["c",182.8,77.4,13,"f"],["c",198.5,99,13,"f"],["c",140,125,48,"B"],["c",140,125,39,""],["c",140,125,34,"f"],["t",140,129,"Ovum","m"],["p","M118 8 Q108 40 128 60 Q132 66 133 72",""],["p","M168 6 Q160 30 168 48 Q172 58 166 70",""],["p","M206 18 Q190 40 178 62",""],["c",134,76,3,"F"],["c",166,74,3,"F"],["c",176,66,3,"F"],["t",212,26,"Sperm",""],["l",210,22,184,40,""],["t",20,128,"Zona",""],["t",10,142,"pellucida",""],["l",50,124,92,123,""],["t",224,110,"Cells of the","s"],["t",224,122,"corona radiata","s"],["l",222,116,208,117,""],["l",222,122,198,139,""],["l",140,159,140,208,""],["t",140,222,"Perivitelline space","m"]]}},
{"id":"neet-2026r-q169","pn":169,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Menstrual cycle","q":"Given below are two statements:\nStatement I: Ovulation is caused by LH surge leading to rupture of Graafian follicles.\nStatement II: Graafian follicle remaining after ovulation transform into corpus luteum and secretes large amount of estrogen.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:","o":["Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect","Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect","Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct","Both Statement I and Statement II are correct"],"c":1,"s":"A rapid rise of LH to its maximum in mid-cycle is the LH surge.\nIt makes the Graafian follicle rupture and release the ovum (ovulation). So Statement I is correct.\nThe rest of the follicle becomes the corpus luteum.\nThe corpus luteum secretes large amounts of progesterone, not estrogen. So Statement II is incorrect."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q110","pn":110,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Sperm structure","q":"Match List - I with List - II.\nList - I: A. Head; B. Middle piece; C. Acrosome; D. Tail\nList - II: (i) Enzymes; (ii) Sperm motility; (iii) Energy; (iv) Genetic material","o":["A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II","A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I","A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV"],"c":0,"s":"The sperm head has an elongated nucleus with the genetic material.\nThe middle piece has many mitochondria, which produce energy for movement.\nThe acrosome is a cap-like structure filled with enzymes that help in fertilisation of the ovum.\nThe tail of the sperm helps sperm motility, needed for fertilisation."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q123","pn":123,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Pregnancy and foetal development","q":"Find the correct statement :\n(A) In human pregnancy, the major organ systems are formed at the end of 12 weeks.\n(B) In human pregnancy the major organ systems are formed at the end of 8 weeks.\n(C) In human pregnancy heart is formed after one month of gestation.\n(D) In human pregnancy, limbs and digits develop by the end of second month.\n(E) In human pregnancy the appearance of hair is usually observed in the fifth month.\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :","o":["A and E only","B and C only","B, C, D and E only","A, C, D and E only"],"c":3,"s":"In a human female's pregnancy:\nBy the end of 12 weeks (1st trimester), most major organ systems are formed (not by the end of 8 weeks).\nAfter one month of pregnancy, the embryo's heart is formed.\nBy the end of the second month, the foetus develops limbs and digits.\nThe first movements of the foetus and appearance of hair on the head are usually seen in the fifth month."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q138","pn":138,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Gametogenesis and menstrual cycle","q":"Consider the following :\nA. The reductive division for the human female gametogenesis starts earlier than that of the male gametogenesis.\nB. The gap between the first meiotic division and the second meiotic division is much shorter for males compared to females.\nC. The first polar body is associated with the formation of the primary oocyte.\nD. Luteinizing Hormone (LH) surge leads to disintegration of the endometrium and onset of menstrual bleeding.\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","o":["A and B are true","A and C are true","B and D are true","B and C are true"],"c":0,"s":"Statements A and B are true; C and D are false.\nThe first polar body is associated with the formation of the secondary oocyte (not the primary oocyte).\nLH surge leads to ovulation.\nDecreased progesterone in the late luteal phase leads to degeneration of the endometrium and onset of menstrual bleeding."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q147","pn":147,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Menstrual cycle","q":"The first menstruation is called :","o":["Menopause","Menarche","Diapause","Ovulation"],"c":1,"s":"The first menstruation begins at puberty and is called menarche.\nOvulation is the release of the secondary oocyte from the mature Graafian follicle.\nIn human beings menstrual cycles cease around 50 years of age; this is menopause.\nDiapause is a state of dormancy or developmental arrest in an organism."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q176","pn":176,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Human Reproduction","st":"Twins","q":"Twins are born to a family that lives next door to you. The twins are a boy and a girl. Which of the following must be true?","o":["They are monozygotic twins.","They are fraternal twins.","They were conceived through in vitro fertilization.","They have 75% identical genetic content."],"c":1,"s":"Fraternal (dizygotic) twins come from 2 separate fertilized eggs. They usually have 2 separate amniotic sacs, placentas and supporting structures.\nIf the twins are a boy and a girl, they are fraternal twins."}
